These terms and conditions govern participation in the World of Hyatt Program by Travel Advisors (defined below) (&ldquo;Travel Advisor Terms&rdquo;). In order to participate in the Program as a travel advisor, an individual must (a) be World of Hyatt Member, (b) be employed by or the owner of an eligible IATA-accredited travel agency and (c) have a valid IATA, TIDS, or CLIA number that can be associated with reservations made on behalf of the advisor&rsquo;s clients (&ldquo;Travel Advisor&rdquo;).&nbsp;Hyatt Priv&eacute; Advisors are also eligible to earn credit in the World of Hyatt Program under these Travel Advisor Terms, as further detailed in the&nbsp;Hyatt Priv&eacute; Program Terms.&nbsp;
Note that these Travel Advisor Terms apply where a Travel Advisor is&nbsp;not&nbsp;making a reservation through the Hyatt Priv&eacute; program. Participation in the Hyatt Priv&eacute; program by eligible travel advisors is subject to separate terms available&nbsp;here. No Travel Advisor may earn credit in the Program through both these Travel Advisor Terms and the Hyatt Priv&eacute; program for any single reservation.
Travel Advisors may earn Tier-Qualifying Night credits in the Program when they arrange for their clients to complete an eligible stay at a participating Hyatt hotel or resort. To do so, a Travel Advisor must make a qualifying reservation for a registered guest (other than the Travel Advisor) paying an Eligible Rate for a stay at a Point Property (subject to the exclusions below) and such reservation must be booked directly through Hyatt.com or the World of Hyatt app or by contacting a Hyatt Global Care Center or the participating Point Property directly (collectively, the &ldquo;Qualifying Booking Channels&rdquo;).
The Travel Advisor must provide their own Program membership number, as well as their IATA, TIDS, or CLIA number, when making the reservation or prior to check-in. (Travel Advisors may not request retroactive credit where their Program membership number has not been applied to a reservation prior to check-in.)
For every five thousand U.S. dollars ($5,000 USD) of Eligible Rate paid &ndash; cumulatively &ndash; by registered guests for [a] qualifying reservation[s] booked by and associated with the Travel Advisor with checkout dates within a single Calendar Year, the Travel Advisor will receive two (2) Tier-Qualifying Night credits in the Program for that Calendar Year&ndash; up to a maximum of sixty (60) Tier-Qualifying Night credits each Calendar Year.
Standard, StandardX, Bunkhouse, Impression by Secrets, Secrets, Dreams, Breathless, Zo&euml;try, Alua, Sunscape, and other Legacy AMR Collection properties (as defined in the Program terms) that participate in the Program are eligible for Travel Advisor earning subject to these Travel Advisor Terms&nbsp;provided that&nbsp;the qualifying reservation at any such property must be made through Hyatt.com, the World of Hyatt app, Hyatt's WeChat mini app, or by contacting a Hyatt Global Care Center. Reservations made directly with the property or through hyattinclusivecollection.com do not constitute a Qualifying Booking Channel and are&nbsp;not&nbsp;eligible. Reservations booked with an Ineligible Rate or through any method other than a Qualifying Booking Channel &ndash; including (except as set forth in the Hyatt Priv&eacute; Program Terms) through any global distribution system (GDS) &ndash; are ineligible.

